: 128000, "output_config.effort": "high", "thinking.display": "summarized", "thinking.type": "adaptive"}, "tools": ["Agent", "Bash", "Edit", "Read", "Skill", "TaskStop", "WebFetch", "Write", "mcp__rwe-search__search_literature"], "tokens": {"cache_write_1h_input": 3827, "cache_write_5m_input": 0, "cache_write_input": 3827, "cached_input": 30985, "input": 34814, "output": 154}, "context": {"bytes": {"conversation": 30668, "other": 423, "system": 35146, "tool_definitions": 14397, "tool_results": 21256}, "measure": "json-utf8-bytes", "total_bytes": 101890}, "gateway_set": ["thinking.display"], "web_search": false, "web_searches": 0, "calls": {"Bash": 1}}}, {"id": "4423fdac-1cbf-5864-ac8e-558fbc87fa29", "at": 1795677573.5850034, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 13276, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "981ce7bf69a2fa61f6fe4b6cbf4353ca", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "ambiguous_order": true, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "9d9d55c4-238a-51d8-84fc-57ce6367086c", "at": 1795677573.5904388, "until": 1795677575.6352587, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 13277, "layer": "worker", "category": "execute", "kind": "tool.pending", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "981ce7bf69a2fa61f6fe4b6cbf4353ca", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": "completed", "ambiguous_order": true, "label": "execute → completed", "repository": null, "tool_call_id": "toolu_01MgUpRdXDCWfzLMA9otmWwK", "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "cd /tmp && rm -rf storywiki2 && git clone -q \"$HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/story-repo.wiki.git\" storywiki2 && cd storywiki2 && git log --oneline | head -5 && git diff HEAD~1 --stat && git diff HEAD~1 | head -150", "shown": {"trace": {"input": [["command", "cd /tmp && rm -rf storywiki2 && git clone -q \"$HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/story-repo.wiki.git\" storywiki2 && cd storywiki2 && git log --oneline | head -5 && git diff HEAD~1 --stat && git diff HEAD~1 | head -150"]], "output": "```console\nf3849f5 Outline rev 2: arms, pre-fixed margin, n-grid, selection in core, compute and data plan, weight on C2/C3\n7362520 Outline revision 1\n Outline.md | 89 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--------------------------\n 1 file changed, 52 insertions(+), 37 deletions(-)\ndiff --git a/Outline.md b/Outline.md\nindex 5ad6398..064f025 100644\n--- a/Outline.md\n+++ b/Outline.md\n@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@\n-# Outline (story-repo, revision 1)\n+# Outline (story-repo, revision 2; answers idea-review #3 in story-repo)\n \n-Built from the objective, the idea's `Brief` (rev. 2) and `prior_work.md`. It says what to test and what each part of the paper must say. It does **not** fix any result: every claim below is a hypothesis with a stated way to fail, and the paper reports whichever outcome the experiments give.\n+Built from the objective, the idea's `Brief` (rev. 4) and `prior_work.md`. It says what to test and what each part of the paper must say. It does **not** fix any result: every claim below is a hypothesis with a stated way to fail, and the paper reports whichever outcome the experiments give.\n \n ## 0. Working title and one-paragraph story\n **\"How much shorter can a prediction-powered interval be? Headroom over PPI++ when labels, unlabeled data and the predictor are all fixed.\"**\n@@ -9,62 +9,77 @@ Prediction-powered inference (PPI, PPI++) turns a fixed predictor into a valid i\n \n **Target parameter (chosen and justified in the paper):** population mean E[Y]. Reason: shared by all nine sets, truth known when a pool is treated as the population, the floor has a closed form. Regression coefficient = extension, only after the mean story is complete.\n \n-## 1. Claims and what carries each\n+## 1. Fixed in advance (before any run): arms, margin, grid, headline form\n+\n+**Arms (named; the ladder and Table 1 use exactly these).**\n+T1 (f only): A0 labels-only (z/t; Wilson and Clopper-Pearson for binary Y); A1 PPI (λ=1, `ppi-python==0.2.3`); A2 PPI++ (same package; the baseline to beat; the free PPI→PPI++ gain V_g(1/N−1/M) sits in this step, and A2 is already the pooled linear estimator); A3 post-stratified PPI on f-bins (post hoc, labels fixed); A4 **PPI++ run on Yhat := ĝ(f)**, ĝ cross-fitted isotonic/spline (nearest published-plus-calibration rival); A5 the **instrument**: pooled cross-fitted calibrated estimator with its own SE (widths of A4 and A5 reported side by side, should agree); A6 A5 with data-driven selection of g among {PPI++, calibrated, flexible} and safeguard, selection inside the repeated-sampling loop on folds separate from variance estimation; A7 estimated floor (cross-fitted fit on the whole pool; not a valid interval, a ceiling on headroom).\n+T2 (f and X; census sets, alphafold indicators): B1 vector PPI++ (g = a + b′(f,X)) and OLS-adjusted mean (strongest linear baseline); B2 GBM-AIPW; B3 calibrated + X; B4 floor with X.\n+\n+**Headline measure and margin (set now; analysis may not move it after seeing results).** Paired width ratio r = width(arm)/width(A2 PPI++) on the same draws, with 95% CI over repetitions. Per cell: **no gain** if the CI of r lies inside [0.98, 1.02]; **gain** if the CI upper bound < 0.95 and the arm is valid (win rule of the Brief); **small / undecided** otherwise. Because width ∝ n^{-1/2}, r also reads as an effective label saving 1 − r² (r=0.95 ≈ 10% fewer labels); the paper states both. For each dataset at its reference n it reports: r of the best valid arm (A5/A6, and B-arms for T2), and r at the estimated floor (A7), both with CIs. The abstract's answer to \"how much shorter\" is the range of these numbers across sets, with the sets where it is no-gain named.\n+\n+**n-grid and N.** Log-spaced n ∈ {30, 100, 300, 1000, 3000, 10000} restricted to what each pool allows (iid with replacement from the pool as population, or n+N ≪ pool, documented per set), plus one *reference n* per set fixed before the runs (the labeled-set size for ballots; for the other sets a value stated in the experiment plan, since they ha\n[truncated for publication]", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "d34374d1-0880-5cde-92ce-05c93139eb30", "at": 1795677574.4020274, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 13280, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "981ce7bf69a2fa61f6fe4b6cbf4353ca", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "360d6632-e004-52b5-b1d5-2fdc5b9d13fa", "at": 1795677574.4096293, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 13281, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "981ce7bf69a2fa61f6fe4b6cbf4353ca", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "45861f47-336c-556d-9b92-6d42faad91f3", "at": 1795677574.4141855, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 13282, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "981ce7bf69a2fa61f6fe4b6cbf4353ca", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "1b61a1d0-db65-5cc0-ba10-451e709d301b", "at": 1795677574.4571095, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 13283, "layer": "worker", "category": "challenge", "kind": "authentication.challenge", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "unknown", "execution_id": "981ce7bf69a2fa61f6fe4b6cbf4353ca", "trust": "system-confirmed", "outcome": "credential-required", "label": "challenge → credent